from (values
('127.753.d.4.D',4,'One way trauma-related stress can affect a responder''s home life is by:','["ending all stress", "causing withdrawal or conflict with loved ones", "lowering bills", "improving all talk"]'::jsonb,1,'Relationships suffer.','original'),
('127.753.d.4.E',3,'Trauma-related stress can lead to poor decisions, missed details and slower reactions on the job. This analyzes the effect on:','["parking", "fashion", "job performance", "weather"]'::jsonb,2,'Stress impairs decisions.','original'),
('127.753.d.4.E',4,'Which job effect can result from unaddressed trauma stress?','["perfect memory", "better teamwork", "faster promotion", "impaired decision-making and attention"]'::jsonb,3,'Cognition suffers under stress.','original'),
('127.753.d.4.F',3,'After a firefighter dies in the line of duty, members may feel grief, guilt and anger. This discusses the psychological impacts of a:','["line of duty death (LODD)", "training exercise", "budget cut", "parade"]'::jsonb,0,'LODD deeply affects the department.','original'),
('127.753.d.4.F',4,'After a LODD, a department commonly provides crew members with:','["no response", "grief support and counseling services", "new patches", "extra hose"]'::jsonb,1,'Support helps survivors.','original'),
('127.753.d.5.A',3,'After a traumatic call, a trained team holds a group meeting to help responders talk through reactions. This is:','["a game", "a fire drill", "Critical Incident Stress Debriefing and management", "a promotion ceremony"]'::jsonb,2,'CISD/CISM supports responders.','original'),
('127.753.d.5.A',4,'The goal of a critical incident stress debriefing is to:','["punish crews", "delete memories", "assign blame", "help responders process an event and reduce stress"]'::jsonb,3,'Debriefings support recovery.','original'),
('127.753.d.5.B',3,'A CISM team includes trained peers, a chaplain and a mental health professional. This describes:','["roles of CISM team members", "roles of mechanics", "roles of dispatchers", "roles of drivers"]'::jsonb,0,'CISM teams are multidisciplinary.','original'),
('127.753.d.5.B',4,'A peer support member on a CISM team is usually:','["a stranger with no training", "a trained fellow first responder", "a vendor", "a salesperson"]'::jsonb,1,'Peers understand the job.','original'),
('127.753.d.5.C',3,'Departments with CISM teams often see better coping, stronger morale and faster recovery. This evaluates the:','["dangers of help", "rules of parking", "benefits of CISM teams in public safety", "costs of ignoring"]'::jsonb,2,'CISM supports responders.','original'),
('127.753.d.5.C',4,'A key benefit of a CISM team is that it can:','["end all calls", "stop all stress", "remove duty", "provide early support and reduce long-term harm"]'::jsonb,3,'Early support helps.','original'),
('127.753.d.5.D',3,'The National Fallen Firefighters Foundation recognizes interventions like one-on-one support and group sessions. These are:','["common CISM interventions", "awards", "hose tests", "fire drills"]'::jsonb,0,'CISM includes several interventions.','original'),
('127.753.d.5.D',4,'A one-on-one peer check-in after a hard call is an example of a:','["parade", "CISM intervention", "pay rule", "training test"]'::jsonb,1,'Individual support is part of CISM.','original'),
('127.753.d.5.E',3,'A department invites spouses to an information night on stress, sleep and where to find help. This explains the importance of:','["skipping events", "keeping secrets", "supporting first responder families", "ignoring families"]'::jsonb,2,'Families feel the stress too.','original'),
('127.753.d.5.E',4,'Supporting responders'' families helps because the family:','["has no role", "is irrelevant", "needs no help", "shares the stress and can provide support"]'::jsonb,3,'Family support is vital.','original'),
('127.753.d.6.E',3,'A Local Assistance and Support Team includes mental health professionals, crisis workers and trained peers. This describes the:','["composition of a LAST", "structure of a pumper", "plan of a station", "list of tools"]'::jsonb,0,'A LAST supports survivors after an LODD.','original'),
('127.753.d.6.E',4,'Members of a LAST typically include:','["only clerks", "mental health professionals and crisis responders", "only drivers", "only chefs"]'::jsonb,1,'Professional support.','original'),
('127.753.d.6.F',3,'After an LODD, a LAST helps the family with funeral logistics, benefits paperwork and counseling. This analyzes the:','["functions of a hose", "functions of a radio", "functions of a LAST", "functions of a ladder"]'::jsonb,2,'A LAST supports survivors.','original'),
('127.753.d.6.F',4,'A LAST''s primary purpose after an LODD is to:','["run drills", "investigate fires", "repair engines", "support survivors and help administer benefits"]'::jsonb,3,'LAST aids survivors.','original'),
('127.753.d.7.A',3,'A candidate for fire department chaplain completes pastoral training, crisis care and department orientation. This describes:','["qualifications of a public safety chaplain", "qualifications of a pilot", "qualifications of a mechanic", "qualifications of a clerk"]'::jsonb,0,'Chaplains need training.','original'),
('127.753.d.7.A',4,'A public safety chaplain is typically trained in:','["gardening", "crisis care and ministry to responders", "metalwork", "accounting"]'::jsonb,1,'Chaplains give spiritual support.','original'),
('127.753.d.7.B',3,'A department offers peer support, counseling referrals and chaplain visits. These are:','["fines", "penalties", "support services for first responders", "chores"]'::jsonb,2,'Agencies provide support.','original'),
('127.753.d.7.B',4,'Which is a support service a first responder organization might provide?','["a fine", "a parking ticket", "a lecture on weather", "an employee assistance program"]'::jsonb,3,'EAPs offer counseling.','original'),
('127.753.d.7.C',3,'A chaplain counsels crew members, visits sick family and officiates at memorials. These are the:','["roles and responsibilities of public safety chaplains", "tasks of dispatchers", "tasks of cooks", "tasks of mechanics"]'::jsonb,0,'Chaplains support people.','original'),
('127.753.d.7.C',4,'A chaplain may serve a department by:','["teaching hose lays", "providing confidential support to members and families", "driving engines", "writing citations"]'::jsonb,1,'Chaplains offer care.','original'),
('127.753.d.7.D',3,'During a mass-casualty event, a chaplain comforts victims'' families and stands by crews. This explains the role of chaplains in:','["paint jobs", "routine parades", "critical incidents and emergencies", "budget meetings"]'::jsonb,2,'Chaplains serve during crises.','original'),
('127.753.d.7.D',4,'At a major disaster, a chaplain commonly helps by:','["fighting the fire", "fixing rigs", "directing traffic", "providing comfort to victims, families and responders"]'::jsonb,3,'Chaplains give emotional and spiritual care.','original'),
('127.753.d.8.A',3,'After a hard season, a firefighter rebounds with support and focus. This explains the concept of:','["resilience", "avoidance", "fatigue", "disregard"]'::jsonb,0,'Resilience is bouncing back.','original'),
('127.753.d.8.A',4,'Resilience helps responders cope with stress by:','["erasing events", "enabling recovery and adaptation after setbacks", "avoiding all stress", "ending calls"]'::jsonb,1,'Resilience supports coping.','original'),
('127.753.d.8.B',3,'Resilient people often have a positive outlook, strong connections and flexible thinking. These are:','["signs of illness", "signs of fatigue", "characteristics of resilient individuals", "signs of danger"]'::jsonb,2,'Resilient people share traits.','original'),
('127.753.d.8.B',4,'One benefit of building resilience is that a person can:','["avoid all challenges", "ignore feelings", "skip work", "handle stress and recover more effectively"]'::jsonb,3,'Resilience helps recovery.','original'),
('127.753.d.8.C',3,'A growth mindset and strong self-awareness help a responder stay steady under pressure. These are:','["internal factors that contribute to resilience", "external costs", "tools", "uniforms"]'::jsonb,0,'Mindset and self-awareness build resilience.','original'),
('127.753.d.8.C',4,'Self-awareness helps resilience because it lets a person:','["skip sleep", "notice stress and respond early", "ignore feelings", "avoid reflection"]'::jsonb,1,'Awareness enables self-care.','original'),
('127.753.d.8.D',3,'A responder builds a support system, uses time management and asks for help when stuck. These are:','["ways to hide", "ways to give up", "strategies to overcome challenges", "ways to quit"]'::jsonb,2,'Strategies support problem-solving.','original'),
('127.753.d.8.D',4,'Which is a healthy strategy for overcoming a challenge?','["isolating", "ignoring it", "blaming others", "reaching out to a trusted support person"]'::jsonb,3,'Support helps.','original'),
('127.753.d.8.E',3,'A medic who worked through a crisis later says it taught him strength and new coping skills. This shows how a crisis can:','["build resiliency and create opportunities for growth", "prove weakness", "end careers", "destroy all growth"]'::jsonb,0,'Crises can lead to growth.','original'),
('127.753.d.8.E',4,'A person who copes well with a past crisis may later:','["lose all skills", "use what they learned to handle new challenges", "avoid all tasks", "fear all stress"]'::jsonb,1,'Experience builds resilience.','original'),
('127.753.d.8.F',3,'A responder uses the steps Stop, Think, Observe, Proceed before acting on a tense call. This is the:','["SMART method", "fire triangle", "STOP method of problem solving", "IDEA method"]'::jsonb,2,'STOP slows down and checks the situation.','original'),
('127.753.d.8.F',4,'In the STOP method, the ''O'' stands for:','["operate", "order", "obey", "observe"]'::jsonb,3,'Observe the situation.','original'),
('127.753.d.8.G',3,'A team uses Identify, Develop, Evaluate and Assess to solve a staffing problem. This is the:','["IDEA method of problem solving", "SMART goal", "STOP method", "fire tetrahedron"]'::jsonb,0,'IDEA is a four-step method.','original'),
('127.753.d.8.G',4,'In the IDEA method, the ''E'' stands for:','["erase", "evaluate", "enter", "exit"]'::jsonb,1,'Evaluate options.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
